#
# The build context of `.clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile`, which ClusterFuzzLite and
# `docs/development.md` build from the checkout's root, is an allowlist:
# everything is left out, then the files the fuzz build reads are let back in,
# then what can sit untracked inside those is left out again. A checkout's
# `.env`, credentials, `.venv/`, caches, logs, worktrees, and `analytics-db/`
# never reach the daemon, and no re-included path lies under a directory that
# is left out, so the operator's `analytics-db/data/` is never even listed.
# Every re-inclusion names its path from the root: a `!**/` pattern would make
# the client walk every directory to look for it.
*
!.clusterfuzzlite/
!fuzz/
!orchestrator/
!LICENSE
!README.md
!poetry.lock
!poetry.toml
!pyproject.toml

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
!orchestrator/service/.env.example
!orchestrator/service/.env.example.advanced
fuzz/**/crash-*
fuzz/**/leak-*
fuzz/**/oom-*
fuzz/**/slow-unit-*
fuzz/**/timeout-*
